                <pb facs="0640" n="528" sameAs="frus:frus1910/pg528"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 24607/30.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Ambassador Reid to the Secretary of State.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1910-05-17"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">May 17, 1910</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1276.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to the department’s cable of
                    the 7th instant, instructing me to express to the British Government the
                    sympathy of the President, Government, and people of the United States at the
                        <pb facs="0641" n="529" xml:id="pg529"/> lamented death of King Edward VII,
                    I have the honor to transmit herewith copies of my notes to the foreign office
                    of the 7th and 8th instant in this sense, together with Sir Edward Grey’s
                    replies of the 11th and 13th instant.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Whitelaw Reid.</hi></signed></closer>





